{"name":"Corsican","hex":"#85ac9d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Corsican","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, from or relating to Corsica, France or the Corsican language."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native or inhabitant of Corsica, France."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Corsican"}],"entries":[{"title":"Corsica","blocks":[{"text":"Corsica is an island in the Mediterranean Sea and one of the 18 regions of France. It is the fourth-largest island in the Mediterranean and lies southeast of the French mainland, west of the Italian Peninsula and immediately north of the Italian island of Sardinia, the nearest land mass. A single chain of mountains makes up two-thirds of the island. As of January 2026, it had a population of 365,636."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Corsica_in_France_2016.svg/330px-Corsica_in_France_2016.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corsica"},{"title":"Corsicans","blocks":[{"text":"The Corsicans are a Romance ethnic group native to the Mediterranean island of Corsica, a territorial collectivity of France."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Blason_de_Corse.svg/330px-Blason_de_Corse.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corsicans"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/The_Mountainous_Spine_of_Corsica.jpeg/500px-The_Mountainous_Spine_of_Corsica.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/The_Mountainous_Spine_of_Corsica.jpeg/1280px-The_Mountainous_Spine_of_Corsica.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/The_Mountainous_Spine_of